# Scraper script
scrape_quadis.py
.aider*

# Raw client deliverables: source zips, unpacked folders, design references,
# working screenshots and the briefs the client sent. Everything the site
# actually ships is committed under public/ — these are the originals we cut
# those from, kept locally only.
#
# This line is also what keeps the client's credentials out of the repo:
# client-assets/briefs/ holds their GoDaddy and Razorpay logins in plaintext.
# Do not narrow this pattern without moving that file somewhere safe first.
client-assets/

# Local-only documentation. docs/Quadis-Audit-1.md IS tracked; these are not.
docs/AWS_DEPLOYMENT_GUIDE.md
docs/Quadis-Frontend-Spec*
docs/quadis-readme-*
docs/pr_*_body.md
/Quadis.mp4

# One-off scratch scripts, kept for reference after their commits landed
scripts/rewrite*.js
scripts/archive/

# Catch-alls for anything new dropped in the project root. Client material
# belongs in client-assets/briefs/, working screenshots in
# client-assets/screenshots/, unplaced photography in client-assets/UNPROCESSED/.
# These are the safety net for the window between a file being saved here and
# being filed — they are NOT the filing system. The root was carrying 22 loose
# images and an 8.7 MB client PDF on 31 Jul; all of it is now filed.
#
# .pdf/.jpg/.png/.docx were added 31 Jul: the original three patterns did not
# cover PDFs, and "Website Changes.pdf" — the client's own change-request
# document — sat tracked in the repo root for five days as a result.
/image*.png
/*.zip
/*.jpeg
/*.jpg
/*.png
/*.pdf
/*.docx

# The 5 Aug 2026 feedback drop. Every pattern above is anchored to the repo
# root, so a client PDF one directory down slips straight past them — which is
# how this bit us before. This folder additionally holds a WhatsApp export
# containing personal, non-work conversation alongside the site feedback, so it
# is not a filing question: it must not enter the history at all.
#
# The three bank logos that came with it ARE committed, as derived site assets
# under public/logos/banks/ — see the note in src/data/logos.ts.
/feedback/

# Agents
..agents/

# Per-agent context files are gone — AGENTS.md at the repo root replaces them,
# and it IS committed. Two private context files existed, they disagreed about
# what was done, and the disagreement cost a database outage and 27 broken
# image paths. A shared contract only works if everyone can see it.
dist-artifact/
